Z||000002||Ronnie||10-16-2001||09:29 PM||||Hey Dave, didn't realize til just now that you're from Punta Gorda. We were down visiting my wifes Aunt there in Ft. Myers, but my wifes sister lives in Port Charlotte!<BR>So, we were all around you!! Too bad , maybe we could have gotten together. Maybe next time we're down that way (once or twice a year)Yeah , keep an eye out for that car. Can't miss it with the wheels painted yellow also.Kindof stands out.We only saw 3 Fieros in our whole trip from Ga.||||reg||6
Z||000003||CoolBlue87GT||10-16-2001||11:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ronnie:<BR><B>Hey Dave, didn't realize til just now that you're from Punta Gorda.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep, Ft Myers is just 20 miles. I've seen a few Fiero's running around the area. <P>The other day I saw a 84 red coupe, it had the dumbest looking plastic 'chrome' wheel covers.<P>It was sad, the paint was neglected. I thought to myself, gosh I wish I have my camera, so I could post for the fourm to see how stupid it looked.<P>I have a few friends in Port Charlotte with Fieros. One has a gold 85 V6 coupe, with a few modifications.<P>The other guy has three, a red 84 coupe, an 85 gold coupe, and a 87 GT he had painted blue. It was a camaro blue, and is a little off the true Fiero blue.<P>Earlier this year, we entered one of our cars in a local show held here in Punta Gorda in Lashley park. Each of us took home a trophy !<P>They were in another class from mine. I took 2nd in my class, was beaten by a 1957 Sliver Gull wing "007 style" Mercedes that was worth 235 thousand dollars !!!  - not bad ?<P>The Group that put the show together told me they were going to create a class just for the Fiero's next year.  <P>I'll end here,  Have you seen my car yet ? How about posting yours ?||||reg||6
Z||000004||Ronnie||10-17-2001||05:43 PM||||Hey Dave. Yes , as a matter of fact, I have seen your car twice.At Daytona in March , and again in Carlisle back in May. I entered my 88GT in Carlisle in the Stock/high mileage class, but think we got there a little too late to get a fair judging on our car.But have since done a little more to the eye appeal of it and have also painted the 88Formula T-Top. Here's a couple of pics for you. Now , take in mind these are not the pristine car that yours is , but both have over 100k miles on them, LOL.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stripes_front_angle_1_1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_paint_side_view_10_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
